Changes made to the original model:
- The 264 encoder matrices of the 24 encoder layers (feed_forward1/2.linear1/2,
  self-attention linear_q, linear_k, linear_v, linear_out, linear_pos, and
  conv.pointwise_conv1/2) were retrained as binary weights {-1, +1} with one
  scale per output row, with quantization-aware and activation-aware training
  (per-frame INT8 activations), distilling from a fine-tuned copy of the
  original model (B0', not released). The codes are stored at one bit per
  weight; the row scales in FP16.
- The prediction network and the joint network were replaced by B0''s and
  stored in INT8 with one FP32 scale per output row; the encoder's
  pre_encode.out was retrained through its INT8 weights and is stored the same
  way.
- All other tensors are stored in FP16, except the feature-extraction window
  and mel filterbank (FP32) and integer BatchNorm counters.
- The weights are distributed as safetensors with manifests and a standalone
  loader (load_kea_b.py) instead of a .nemo archive; compat/ holds the same
  weights in kea-b 0.0's format. The tokenizer files and the model
  configuration are unchanged copies from the original .nemo archive.

Training data (audio). Training targets: for the recorded corpora, transcripts
produced by the label teacher below (the single-distant-microphone AMI audio
took the label of its headset recording); for Common Voice, its read sentences;
for the synthetic speech, the generated sentences it was synthesized from.
The recorded corpora's and Common Voice's targets went through the label-cleaning
pass described in TRAINING.md.
Other human transcripts were used only for filtering.
